# Soldier of Darkness

## Lore

Also called a Harbinger of Chaos. This is a form of pact magic not seen in the world for seventy thousand years, and it belongs to the Kkairojan Minotaurs alone. Like the tribe''s witches, a Soldier of Darkness gives himself to the Old Ones without reservation or term. What he gets in return is not a witch''s gifts but a warrior''s: a body hardened and quickened past anything natural, strength of the supernatural kind, and a short list of spells suited to finding enemies and breaking them.

The Soldiers are the armed hand of the Old Ones'' cults. They guard the priests and Disciples, keep the worshippers in line, and hunt down anyone who stands in the way of the awakening. About one Kkairojan in three bears the mark, which is easy to see: skin gone the blue-grey of steel and eyes that glow like coals.

## Alignment

Evil. The tribe is almost wholly diabolic or miscreant, and the pledge is to the Old Ones.

## GM Notes

The book gives this class its powers and its experience table and nothing else - no skills, no fighting style, no starting gear or coin. Until that gap is ruled on, settle a Soldier''s training at the table.

The Hit Point bonus and the natural A.R. of 15 are what the race entry means when it prints, on its Hit Points and Natural Armor Rating lines only, that the figure is higher for a Soldier of Darkness. The supernatural P.S. is not part of that: it comes from the Soldier''s own Bonuses bullet.

The spells of choice at even levels are wizard spells of levels one to four only, however high the Soldier climbs.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'soldier-of-darkness');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'soldier-of-darkness';

